        "geometry_type": "approximate",
        "digitized_from": "Real-gap-fragment technique: bbox.difference(street buffer).difference(already-tracked polygons) between 3rd St and Illinois St, south of 16th St, extended down to Mariposa St. The owner directly identified this whole real-gap fragment as capturing two separate real buildings, not one, and directed cutting it at the visible gap between the two rooflines in Esri satellite imagery (lat 37.76578).",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-20: the owner corrected the block_inventory rows for 33 and 34, which had pointed at 490/499 Illinois Street -- real buildings, but 82-84m from 3rd St, too far to be the blocks the OCII plan drawing shows bordering 3rd St directly (they actually front Illinois St, matching their own address). The real 33/34 strip (between 3rd St and Illinois St) had no tracked record at all. This is the south building (34): the real-gap-fragment split south of the visible gap between the two rooflines, extending down to the real Mariposa St curb line -- 9,240 sqm (corrected from an initial 5,303 sqm that wrongly clipped the building at an early analysis-window edge rather than its real south extent).",
        "accuracy_caveat": "REAL BUILDING, APPROXIMATE BOUNDARY -- a real, standing structure clearly visible in Esri satellite imagery (not open land), but its own name/address/operator are NOT confirmed by any source checked in this pass -- flagged here rather than guessed. Boundary is the real-gap-fragment's own traced edge (following the street buffer's curb radius), not a hand-traced or surveyed building footprint.",
        "notes": "OCII plan block 34. Between 3rd St and Illinois St, south of block 33, down to Mariposa St. Name/operator not yet confirmed.",
